WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.305
Start by preparing a controller that you
can inspect. In an unconfigured

00:00:04.305 --> 00:00:08.372
Studio, choose Set up workspace and create
suite. You can create the

00:00:08.372 --> 00:00:12.916
controller environment, select an existing
project, or open the setup guide.

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:16.808
Package downloads require an explicit
installation confirmation.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:20.452
The controller provides PerfChecker and
its measurement tools.

00:00:20.583 --> 00:00:24.997
The package being measured still needs its
own dependencies, and existing

00:00:24.997 --> 00:00:29.169
test items need their test dependencies in
the selected runner. After

00:00:29.169 --> 00:00:33.221
setup, inspect Runner Project and the
resolved PerfChecker version.

00:00:33.352 --> 00:00:37.481
For an MCP connection, add HTTP
deliberately to the controller.

00:00:37.481 --> 00:00:41.216
Pluto uses a separate project with the
qualified notebook

00:00:41.216 --> 00:00:44.821
dependencies. Opening Studio gives you the
next action.

00:00:44.952 --> 00:00:48.624
It does not request measurements or
install an agent. A clear

00:00:48.624 --> 00:00:52.838
environment selection makes the later
result much easier to reproduce.
